  "context": "Low priority: publish already fails closed on any residual leak. Verification rubric: tests for each closed case, allowlist tests unchanged, comment-policy and ruff, PR merged with green CI.\n\nBATCH DECISIONS (2026-11-09, owner-delegated defaults): (a) CLOSE: a custom $HOME is added as a leak-scan root when it is set and is not a neutral placeholder. (b) CLOSE: anonymize_plans_payload sanitizes top-level errors text like the other text fields. (c) ACCEPT AND DOCUMENT: paths outside the known roots (e.g. /srv/...) stay flagged only when configured; record this in the privacy docs with the configured-roots escape hatch; do not widen the known root list without evidence from real captured plans. Each closed case needs allowlist false-positive tests unchanged plus a publish dry-run smoke. Depends on the detector and sanitizer code merged in PR #4054; sequence after the loader item only if they touch the same file. GUARDRAILS: stored fingerprints are never recomputed; never print leaked path values in diagnostics; do not widen the detector to every absolute path (owner decision 2026-11-08); fail-closed publish behavior stays; private non-anonymized exports unchanged; no hosted data deletion or history rewrite. Verification rubric: (1) reproduce with a failing test or script before editing; (2) focused suites pass via uv run -- python -m pytest -n 0; (3) make comment-policy-check and ruff on touched files; (4) the runtime smoke named in acceptance is recorded in the PR body; (5) one final batch PR merges with green CI and a passing oracle review.",
